# Z (hand-back, last card step): the node agent is started. The agent loads its placement only after the platform's release step creates the serving container, so Z waits for it (up to 30 minutes)
# and the OPERATOR runs the release step during that wait with the owner's admin key; the key is never in a script. Z READS PASS when its log has 'node agent after start: active', whether the run
# ended green or timed out waiting for the container. Before it: the kill-switch files (prefix-reuse.off, levern.off) on the hub mount are RESTORED to the state recorded before A0X0 (a switch production set stays set; a file the owner approved moving aside for the window goes back; a file the window's own drills wrote is gone). Never delete production's switch.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the third session of 2026-10-08/09 (s0809) (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it). ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags
# and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its default); tp4-serve-10 is the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box:
# the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run. NO profile of this pack carries a digest or an audit (QWEN_PREFIX_DIGESTS, QWEN_PREFIX_AUDIT, the lever audits): test_tp4_session_0809 pins that.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status agentstart
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
